      }
    }
  ],
  "limits": {
    "ticks": 3600,
    "decisions": 10
  },
  "solution": [
    "goto <${dx},0,${dz - 2}> dist=1",
    "mine clay n=${n} tool=iron_shovel",
    "goto <0,0,0> dist=0"
  ],
  "solution_ticks": 1200,
  "notes": "One layer of source water above clay, with solid stone below and dry walkable banks on all sides. Mining creates at most two-block-deep water pockets. The bot starts and respawns dry. Each clay block drops four balls without Silk Touch; pickup and the final return exercise shallow-water pathfinding. From the spawn the clay under the water is hidden by the bank (no line of sight): the bot has to walk to the edge to see it."
}
